      "writtenOn": "2023-07-27T14:56:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah this isn\u0027t intended to be any stronger than what the flag guard guidelines say (\"Every deprecation/addition of web platform APIs\"). Perhaps it would be clearer to say that any I2S requires a flag, but PSAs are up to the individuals judgement? Every \"deprecation/addition to web platform APIs\" requires a flag, so I wouldn\u0027t want to imply that flags are only \"encouraged\" for every I2S. But PSAs tend to be trivial and there\u0027s a lot of judgement around whether to even send a PSA or not, so I don\u0027t personally see a need for a requirement tying flag guarding and PSAs.",
